	(text "2. MASTER MAINS RELAY  (cuts LIVE to all motors + valves when chain breaks)"(exclude_from_sim no)(at 177.80 25.40 0)(effects(font(size 2.0 2.0))(justify left top))(uuid "579cb7a7-c196-4a9e-8eee-f5cafb068ffa"))
	(text "3. STATUS BACK TO CONTROLLER  (12V -> ~3.0V for the MCP23017)"(exclude_from_sim no)(at 25.40 137.16 0)(effects(font(size 2.0 2.0))(justify left top))(uuid "df2e01df-3473-4240-953c-53d7541bcbd7"))
	(text "4. RELAY INPUT PULL-DOWNS  (relays stay OFF while ESP32 boots or if the ribbon is unplugged)"(exclude_from_sim no)(at 177.80 137.16 0)(effects(font(size 2.0 2.0))(justify left top))(uuid "4e9c0ce1-445b-47ea-8675-49a7fe19a36c"))
	(text "5. SURGE PROTECTION"(exclude_from_sim no)(at 25.40 213.36 0)(effects(font(size 2.0 2.0))(justify left top))(uuid "a0d3b730-136b-46e0-8e50-102ab0992729"))
	(text "HOW IT WORKS\n- Every relay coil is fed from +12V_RLY. Q3 only turns on when ALL of these are true:\n    E-stop not pressed (J32 closed)  AND  high-pressure switch OK (J33 closed)  AND\n    SAFE_EN high from the controller (firmware says OK AND the TPS3823 watchdog has not tripped).\n- Break any link and every relay drops: compressor, pump and fan stop, all valves close, K12 cuts mains (LIVE_SW).\n- K12 has no CPU control of its own: it is ON whenever the chain is healthy. Firmware turns SAFE_EN on first,\n  then the loads, so K12 always switches with no load (long contact life).\n- D19 catches the coil spike when the chain opens. R33-R43 hold the ULN2803 inputs low.\n- ESTOP_OK / HP_OK let the screen say which link is open (if E-stop is open, HP_OK also reads open).\n- K12 needs its own 16A relay (ALZ22B12 or equivalent). Mains tracks: keep 6mm+ from low voltage."(exclude_from_sim no)(at 177.80 205.74 0)(effects(font(size 1.27 1.27))(justify left top))(uuid "3fc1ea9c-da2d-48b8-ad53-6082b59610e1"))
